/**
 * requestFacets.heldout7.spec.ts — seventh facet set: the BLIND check of the
 * computed-value frames (Copilot standard-setup retest, 2026-10-02). 60 items
 * (36 EN + 24 JA; value questions phrased as return/output/produce/evaluate/
 * calculate, same-word negatives, and value+other mixes) generated by EVO-X2
 * in a fresh context with a differently worded prompt over 10+ domains (no
 * payments/e-commerce, measured fixtures' identifiers banned). Labels
 * adjudicated by the orchestrator BEFORE scoring (en-16, en-18: flow, callers
 * only tolerated; ja-15: callers, flow tolerated; ja-21: value+flow, callers
 * tolerated). The module was never tuned against this set: scored ONCE, after
 * the last change, recorded as is.
 *
 * BLIND RESULT (2026-10-02): value recall 0.40 -> 0.65 with precision 1.00 ->
 * 1.00 (pre-change vs final extractor); condition/callers/flow identical in
 * both. Remaining value misses, kept as misses: bare code-object imperatives
 * ("Evaluate `f()` for ...", "Compute `g()` for ..."), "the return value of
 * `h()` for <inputs>" and 返り値 (the return-value guard), and JA phrasings
 * without a code subject directly before の結果/出力 (の出力結果は, 評価結果を,
 * 出力は何になりますか, 結果を計算し, 計算してください).
 *
 * Floors are a regression guard just under that blind result, not a target.
 * Tuning the module against this set's misses turns it into a development
 * set -- say so here if that ever happens, and measure on a new unseen set.
 */
